  h = HOST shared objects the payload process opened. Objects the
  artefact brought with it are counted separately and are in
  per-environment.txt -- for both arms those are the bundled ld.so,
  libc and the application's own libraries.

  ⭐ cold is one chroot enter with a COLD dwarfs mount, guaranteed by
  reaping the rootfs first. warm is (six invocations - cold) / 5, taken
  inside ONE enter with the mount left alive -- which is what a real
  user gets and what the first version of this instrument destroyed by
  reaping between runs. experiments/40-'s noise floor applies: a
  difference at or under it is "no difference measurable".

